>
> Finally, just a question for curiosity: l looked in the manual, but l didn't find any stan functions for Bernoulli(Phi) ( but I found bernoulli_logit_log); is there no implementation for it?

bernoulli_log is the function.  Every probability function
you can write as

  y ~ foo(theta)

has a corresponding function

  foo_log(y,theta).

When you get a chance to study the marginalization chapter and
if you still have questions, we're happy to help.

