Hi Stan,

I'm translating a Jags program concerning elastic net in probit regression into Stan language.

The model I'm dealing with is the following( code at bottom):

The background is the probit regression with hierarchical priors on hyperparameters:

likelihood : Y | beta0,beta,x,sigma is a "function"(likelihood)  L(y;g(beta0+beta*x),sigma)

 where beta 0 is the intercept  and sigma is equal to 1

beta0~ normal(0,100)   with standard deviation= 100; // normal prior on the intercept

a1 ~exponential(mu1);

a2~ exponential(mu2);

beta0~normal(0,sd_b0);

hierarchical formulation:

tau~ gamma (shape,scaleg) T[1,];

beta~ normal(0.0,sqrt((tau[j]-1)/(tau[j]*a2)));

 with shape given in the data block and scalet, a parameter related to a1 and a2, represents the scale of a gamma distribution ;

data{

                               int<lower=0> N; // number of individuals

                               int<lower=0> k; // number of predictors

                               matrix[N,k] x; // matrix of predictors

                               int <lower=0,upper=1> Y[N];  // binary data

                               real mu1;

                               real mu2;

                               real<lower=0> sd_b0;

                               real<lower=0> shape;

}

parameters{

                                               real beta0;

                                               vector[p] beta;

                                               vector[p] tau;

                                               real a1;

                                               real a2;

                               }

transformed parameters{

    real<lower=0> scalet;

scalet<-pow(a1,2)/(8*a2);

}

model{

real sm1;

vector[N] muu;

vector[N] z;

a1 ~exponential(mu1);

a2~ exponential(mu2);

beta0~normal(0,sd_b0);

for(j in 1:k){

                tau[j]~ gamma (shape,scalet) T[1,];

              // truncated gamma distribution:I'm interested in defining it in   the interval (1,+ Infinity)

            // Gamma distribution I'm consider is parametrized by Gamma(a,b) where a is the shape and b the scale

           //In this example, Gamma is given by Gamma(0.5, (8*a1)/(a1^2))

          //Thus, according to the expression of the distribution of the manual, the second parameter of Gamma should be the inverse of (8*a1)/(a1^2)

                beta[j]~ normal(0.0,sqrt((tau[j]-1)/(tau[j]*a2)));

}

// likelihood    I translated what I wrote in jags  :

