On Tuesday, January 20, 2015 at 5:58:33 PM UTC-5, John Sutton wrote:
> I don't understand what the "to vector..." statement does, since it doesn't seem to correspond with the description in the latest manual.

The normal sampling statement only permits vectors or scalars to be on the left-hand side. So, to_vector() just stacks the input matrix columnwise and then each of the elements is assumed to be iid normal with mean 0 and standard deviation 2.

> xmat is an NxD matrix with ones in the first column.
>
> Alas, this doesn't run, and generates the following error message:
>
> > Error in (function (x)  :
> >   no function to return from, jumping to top level
> > Error in eval(expr, envir, enclos) :
> >   mismatch in dimension declared and found in context; processing stage=data initialization; variable name=xmat; position=1; dims declared=(21855,4); dims found=(21855,5)
> > failed to create the sampler; sampling not done

This means that the thing in R that corresponds to xmat in Stan had 5 columns but Stan was expecting it to have only 4 columns.

Ben

