Date: Wed, 28 Jan 2015 00:32:26 +0000
Subject: Re: use the posterior as the prior
Message-ID: <syIX5PoHSEg.4IQ-45cN_psJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <syIX5PoHSEg.HH2r96zqi3QJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <syIX5PoHSEg.HH2r96zqi3QJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/syIX5PoHSEg/m/4IQ-45cN_psJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Assuming your data x follows blah distribution and you sampled parameter alpha K times in previous phase.
Use previous sampled parameters as another data to build a posterior distribution.

pseudo codes here:
functions{
  real update_alpha_log(posterior_alpha, vector[M] prior_alpha[K]){
    ...
  }
  real blah_log(vector[N] x, vector[M] alpha){
    ...
  }
}
data{
  bool build_posterior_from_prior;
  vector[M] prior_alpha[K];
  vector[N] x;
}
parameters{
  vector[M] posterior_alpha;
}
model{
  if(build_posterior_from_prior){
    posterior_alpha ~ update_alpha(prior_alpha);
  }
  x ~ blah(posterior_alpha);
}

